---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout basePath="/v1" 
  title="Your Life Transformation Report | Ask Astro Raja"
  description="A highly personalized, deep-dive Vedic astrology report analyzing your inner and outer worlds, karmic loops, and daily systems."
>

  <!-- Control Panel for Web Viewers (Hidden in Print) -->
  <div class="print:hidden max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-6 mb-8 mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-brand-border flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center gap-4">
    <div>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-1">Your Report is Ready</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-brand-text-muted">You can save this report directly as a high-quality PDF.</p>
    </div>
    <button onclick="window.print()" class="px-6 py-3 bg-brand-saffron text-white font-bold rounded-xl hover:bg-brand-saffron-dark transition-colors flex items-center gap-2 shadow-sm">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/><line x1="12" x2="12" y1="15" y2="3"/></svg>
      Download PDF
    </button>
  </div>

  <!-- PDF Document Container -->
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto bg-white sm:rounded-[2rem] sm:shadow-sm sm:border border-brand-border/40 p-8 sm:p-16 mb-24 print:shadow-none print:border-none print:p-0 print:m-0 print:max-w-none text-brand-navy bg-white">
    
    <!-- PAGE 1: COVER & FOUNDATION -->
    <div class="print-page-break pb-12">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="text-center mb-16 pt-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4 tracking-tight uppercase">Life Transformation Report</h1>
        <h2 class="text-3xl text-brand-purple font-bold mb-6">MOHANRAAJ</h2>
        <p class="text-xl text-brand-text italic mb-2">Simbha Raasi (சிம்மம்) + Kanni Lagnam (கன்னி) + Puram 4th Padam (பூரம்)</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-text-muted font-medium">The King Trapped in the Perfectionist's Prison</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 1 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">1. ASTRO FOUNDATION</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10 border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/4">Aspect</th>
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-3/8">Raasi — Simbham</th>
              <th class="p-4 w-3/8">Lagnam — Kanni</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-brand-text text-sm md:text-base">
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Sign</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Leo (சிம்மம்)</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Virgo (கன்னி)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Symbol</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Lion (சிங்கம்)</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Virgin / Maiden (கன்னி)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Element</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Fire (நெருப்பு)</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Earth (பூமி)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Ruling Planet</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Sun / Surya (சூரியன்)</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Mercury / Budhan (புதன்)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Nakshatra</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Puram 4th Padam (பூரம்) — Ruled by Venus. The royal star of luxury, creativity, and public presence.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50"></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Core Nature</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Pride, leadership, warmth, generosity, needs admiration, dramatic, big-hearted, craves recognition</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Analytical, perfectionist, detail-oriented, critical, service-minded, anxious, over-thinks everything</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Thinking Style</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Feels grand, thinks big, wants to be the center. Decisions come from pride and heart. "I deserve this."</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Analyzes every angle, finds every flaw, worries about every detail. "Is this good enough? What if there's a mistake?"</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Prose -->
      <div class="space-y-6 text-brand-text leading-relaxed">
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg mb-2">Symbol connection — The Lion and The Maiden:</h4>
          <p>The Lion is the king of the jungle. It walks with majesty, demands respect, and expects to be admired. It was BORN to rule. The Maiden is meticulous, careful, humble, always checking, always correcting, always worried about imperfection. Now put them in one body. Inside, Mohanraaj feels like a king — he KNOWS he's meant for something great. He has the vision, the warmth, the leadership instinct. Outside, the Maiden makes him second-guess every step, over-analyze every decision, and paralyze himself with perfectionism before the Lion can even roar.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg mb-2">Puram 4th Padam — The Royal Star in the House of Emotion:</h4>
          <p>Puram nakshatra is the star of royalty, creativity, and public life. It's ruled by Venus, giving Mohanraaj a natural love for beauty, comfort, art, and meaningful connections. The 4th padam falls in Cancer navamsa — adding an emotional, nurturing, family-oriented depth to the royal energy. This means Mohanraaj doesn't just want success — he wants success that MEANS something. He wants to build something his family is proud of. He wants recognition not for ego but for validation that his life MATTERS. When this validation doesn't come, the Lion's pride is wounded and the Maiden's anxiety takes over.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="my-8 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron pl-6 py-2">
        <p class="text-xl font-serif font-medium text-brand-navy italic leading-snug">"I am a king who forgot his crown — because the perfectionist inside keeps telling him it's not polished enough to wear."</p>
      </blockquote>

    </div> <!-- End Page 1 -->

    <!-- PAGE 2: CORE TRUTH & PROFILE -->
    <div class="print-page-break pb-12 pt-8">
      
      <!-- Section 2 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">2. CORE COMBINATION TRUTH</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12 border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/2">INNER WORLD (Simbha Raasi)</th>
              <th class="p-4 w-1/2">OUTER APPROACH (Kanni Lagnam)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-brand-text text-sm md:text-base">
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Feels like a leader — born to shine, guide, and inspire</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Appears analytical, careful, self-doubting, overly cautious</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Craves recognition: "See me. Value me. Admire me."</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Hides from the spotlight because "I'm not ready yet"</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Thinks big — grand visions, majestic plans</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Thinks small — micro-details, flaws, risks, what could go wrong</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Generous, warm, big-hearted</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Critical, judgmental — of self first, then others</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Wants to take bold action and lead</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Over-analyzes until the moment passes. Then regrets.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4">Needs love, admiration, and emotional warmth</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">Pushes people away with criticism and emotional distance</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4">Deep down: "I am special. I have a gift."</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50">On the surface: "Who am I to think I'm special?"</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-12">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg mb-3">The Conflict:</h4>
        <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-6">This is one of the most PAINFUL combinations in the zodiac — because the gap between what Mohanraaj feels inside and what he shows outside is enormous. Inside, the Lion ROARS. He knows he's meant for greatness. He can feel it. He can see the vision. Outside, the Maiden whispers: "But what if you fail? What if it's not perfect? What if people judge you?" The Lion wants to leap. The Maiden wants to check the landing spot 47 times first. By the time the analysis is done, the opportunity is gone. Then the Lion is wounded — not by failure, but by the regret of never having tried.</p>
        <p class="text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-6">The deepest pain: Mohanraaj is MISUNDERSTOOD. People see the Virgo exterior — quiet, analytical, critical, reserved. They have no idea that inside there is a Lion starving for recognition, love, and a chance to shine. He feels lonely not because nobody is around — but because nobody sees the real him.</p>
        <blockquote class="my-8 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron pl-6 py-2">
          <p class="text-xl font-serif font-medium text-brand-navy italic leading-snug">"The world sees a quiet analyst. Inside lives a roaring king. The tragedy is not that I can't lead — it's that I won't let myself."</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 3 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">3. CHARACTER PROFILE</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border bg-green-700 w-1/2">STRENGTHS</th>
              <th class="p-4 bg-red-700 w-1/2">WEAKNESSES (Uncomfortable Truths)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-brand-text text-sm md:text-base">
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Natural leader — people WANT to follow him when he steps up</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Rarely steps up because he's waiting to be "ready." Ready never comes.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Brilliant analytical mind — sees details others miss</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Uses analysis as a disguise for fear. "I'm still researching" = "I'm too scared to start."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Deeply creative — Puram gives artistic, aesthetic sensibility</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Creates in private but never shares because it's "not good enough yet." The world never sees the gift.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Extremely loyal and devoted to family</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Devotion becomes suffocation. Expectations become resentment when unreciprocated.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">High standards — everything he does has quality</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Standards so high that nothing ever meets them — including himself. Perfectionism is his prison.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Warm and generous when comfortable</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Cold and critical when stressed. The warmth vanishes and the Virgo critic takes over.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Can see the big picture AND the small details</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Gets lost in small details and forgets the big picture. Spends hours on fonts while the business burns.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-green-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 border-r border-brand-border">Deeply wants to serve and help others</td>
              <td class="p-4 bg-red-50/30">Helps everyone except himself. Self-neglect is his default setting.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

    </div> <!-- End Page 2 -->

    <!-- PAGE 3: IMPACT & LOOPS -->
    <div class="print-page-break pb-12 pt-8 print-avoid-break">
      
      <!-- Section 4 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">4. LIFE AREA IMPACT</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-12 border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/5">Life Area</th>
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-2/5">How this combination shows up</th>
              <th class="p-4 w-2/5">The hidden cost</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-brand-text text-sm md:text-base">
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Career</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">No clear direction. Leo inside wants to lead but Virgo outside keeps saying "not yet." Overqualified for his current reality. Knows he can do more but can't start because nothing feels perfect enough.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50">Years pass. Talent is wasted. The Lion gets smaller every year it doesn't roar. Potential without execution is the cruelest form of poverty.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Money</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Leo wants luxury and comfort (especially with Puram's Venus influence). Virgo is anxious about every rupee. The result: wants expensive things but feels guilty buying them. Earns inconsistently because career has no direction.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50">Financial anxiety is constant. Not because he can't earn — but because he never commits to ONE path long enough for it to pay. Money instability feeds the Virgo anxiety machine.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Marriage</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Leo wants to be admired and appreciated by partner. Virgo makes him critical and hard to please. He sees every flaw in the relationship and points it out. Wife feels she can never be good enough.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50">Emotional distance. Wife stops trying because the bar is impossibly high. Leo feels unloved. Virgo blames the wife. Nobody wins.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Family</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Deep sense of duty. But feels unappreciated. Does everything for family, expects recognition, rarely gets it.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50">Quiet resentment builds. "I sacrifice everything and nobody notices." The Virgo keeps score. The Leo keeps getting hurt.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold bg-slate-50">Health & Mind</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Virgo rules the nervous system. Overthinking = acidity, gut problems, sleep issues, anxiety symptoms. Brutal inner critic attacking a sensitive ego.</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border bg-slate-50/50">The body whispers first, then shouts, then screams. Mental exhaustion. Loneliness from feeling misunderstood. Nobody sees the Lion.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 5 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">5. CORE LIFE LOOP</h3>
      <p class="text-brand-text mb-4 italic">This is the cycle that keeps Mohanraaj trapped. Not fate. Not karma. A pattern he keeps feeding.</p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8 border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-12 text-center">#</th>
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/3">Stage</th>
              <th class="p-4 w-auto">What's really happening</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-brand-text text-sm md:text-base">
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center bg-slate-50">1</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border">The Lion's vision appears</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Leo sees a grand possibility. A business idea. A career move. A creative project. The heart KNOWS this is right. Excitement builds. "This could be my moment."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center bg-slate-50">2</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border">The Maiden starts analyzing</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Virgo takes over. "But what about this risk? What about that detail? What if it fails? Let me research more. Let me plan more. Let me make sure it's PERFECT before I start."</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center bg-slate-50">3</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border">Analysis paralysis</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Weeks turn into months. Still planning. Still perfecting. Still "researching." The window of opportunity starts closing. Others who are less talented but more decisive move ahead.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center bg-slate-50">4</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border">The Lion's pride is wounded</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">Sees others succeeding with LESS talent. "I'm better than them — why are THEY succeeding?" Frustration. Jealousy. Self-pity. The Lion feels humiliated by his own inaction.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-brand-border bg-red-50/30">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center">5</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border">Self-criticism spiral</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border">The Virgo judge turns inward. "You're a fraud. You'll never do it. Who are you to think you're special?" The inner critic destroys what's left of the Lion's confidence.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="bg-red-50/50">
              <td class="p-4 font-bold text-center">6</td>
              <td class="p-4 font-bold border-l border-brand-border text-red-900">Retreat and repeat</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-l border-brand-border text-red-900">Gives up. Goes quiet. Retreats into routine. Until the next vision appears — and the cycle starts over. The graveyard of unexecuted ideas grows. The Lion gets smaller.</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      
      <blockquote class="my-8 border-l-4 border-brand-saffron pl-6 py-2">
        <p class="text-xl font-serif font-medium text-brand-navy italic leading-snug">"I am not failing because I lack talent. I am failing because I won't let imperfect talent see the light of day. My perfectionism is not quality control — it is fear wearing a lab coat."</p>
      </blockquote>

    </div> <!-- End Page 3 -->

    <!-- PAGE 4: KARMA & SOLUTIONS -->
    <div class="print-page-break pb-12 pt-8 print-avoid-break">
      
      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">6. KARMIC PATTERN ANALYSIS</h3>
      <p class="text-brand-text mb-8">These are not curses from past lives. These are behavioral grooves carved so deep they feel like destiny.</p>
      
      <div class="space-y-6 text-brand-text leading-relaxed mb-12">
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-purple text-lg mb-1">Karmic loop #1: The Uncrowned King</h4>
          <p>Know you're meant to lead &rarr; wait until you're "perfectly ready" &rarr; never feel ready &rarr; watch less talented people take the crown &rarr; feel bitter and wounded &rarr; criticize yourself and them &rarr; retreat &rarr; wait again &rarr; repeat. Mohanraaj's core karma: he keeps abdicating the throne because the crown doesn't look perfect enough. Meanwhile, imperfect kings are ruling the world he was meant for.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-purple text-lg mb-1">Karmic loop #2: The Invisible Giver</h4>
          <p>Give to family and others &rarr; expect recognition and gratitude &rarr; don't get it (because Leo expectations are VERY high) &rarr; feel unseen and unvalued &rarr; become critical and withdrawn &rarr; people distance themselves &rarr; feel even more invisible &rarr; give more to compensate &rarr; repeat. The Lion gives like a king but tracks like an accountant. When the books don't balance, resentment poisons the generosity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-brand-light-bg p-6 rounded-xl border border-brand-border">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-brand-navy text-lg mb-2">Root cause:</h4>
          <p>Mohanraaj's inner Leo says: "I am the Sun. I was born to shine." His outer Virgo says: "But what if the light isn't bright enough? What if people see the flaws?" This battle has been running his entire life. The karma is simple: SHINE ANYWAY. Imperfectly. Messily. Humanly. The world doesn't need a perfect king. It needs a present one.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 font-serif italic font-medium text-brand-saffron-dark text-lg">"My karma is not suffering. My karma is the refusal to shine until conditions are perfect. Conditions will NEVER be perfect. The Sun doesn't wait for a cloudless sky. It rises every day regardless."</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6 border-b-2 border-brand-saffron pb-2">8. WHAT MUST BE LET GO</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10 border border-brand-border rounded-xl">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-brand-navy text-white text-sm">
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/5">Let Go Of</th>
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/4">Wrong Belief</th>
              <th class="p-4 border-r border-brand-navy-light w-1/4">The Truth</th>
              <th class="p-4 w-auto">Daily Practice</th>
            </tr>
